1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Agent memory is valuable, but it should not be trapped inside one product.

2
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:31,000
This privacy-first adapter starts with a genuine Codex session and keeps only
reusable user and assistant messages.

3
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:44,000
System prompts, reasoning, tool calls, credentials, and transport metadata
remain excluded.

4
00:00:44,000 --> 00:01:00,000
The session becomes Open Knowledge Format: plain, readable Markdown that can be
inspected, versioned, and carried anywhere.

5
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:17,000
Privacy tests pass, and all three golden questions have exact source-to-OKF
recall parity.

6
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:34,000
Memanto's official dry run maps all four OKF nodes into four context memories.

7
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:52,000
The live cloud import completes with four memories imported and zero failures.

8
00:01:52,000 --> 00:02:22,000
After migration, the expected answer ranks first for all three validation
questions. The agent has not forgotten.

9
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:43,000
All four memories can be exported from Memanto back into readable OKF.

10
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:58,000
Codex session. Portable OKF. Memanto memory. Portable OKF again.
The agent keeps its knowledge, and the user keeps ownership.
